    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **34 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule. The `membershipTier` is a read-time derived property (`Owner.getMembershipTier()`), so I gave the entity a stored snapshot of household size at creation:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `householdSize` field (`@Column(name = \"household_size\")`) with getter/setter, and updated `getMembershipTier()` to return `\"GOLD\"` when `householdSize >= 3`, before falling back to the existing SILVER/BRONZE logic.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 When an owner is created, it now records the household member count: `householdMembers.size() + 1` for a shared household, or `1` otherwise. This captures \"members after this create\" as a per-owner snapshot, matching the spec's \"after this create\" wording (the third member of a shared household sees size 3 \u2192 GOLD).\n\n3. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added the `household_size INTEGER` column, since the test profile uses `ddl-auto=none` with `schema.sql`.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Updated the `membershipTier` description to document the GOLD rule.\n\nThe new `Cp23Tests` (three-member household \u2192 GOLD) passes, and the existing SILVER/BRONZE (`Cp15`), household-id (`Cp11`), and namesake (`Cp13`) tests remain green \u2014 a single-member household has `householdSize = 1`, so those rules are untouched.",
